# Importing Required Libraries

In this step, the necessary Python libraries are imported for:
- Data analysis
- Data visualization
- Chart creation
"""

import pandas as pd
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
import seaborn as sns

# show charts clearly
plt.rcParams['figure.figsize'] = (10,5)

"""# Loading the Dataset

The sales dataset is loaded into the notebook using Pandas.

This dataset contains business sales information such as:
- Orders
- Products
- Sales
- Profit
- Categories
- Regions

The dataset will be used for further analysis and visualization.
"""

df = pd.read_csv('/content/Sample - Superstore.csv', encoding='latin1')

df.head()

df.info()

df.describe()

"""# Data Cleaning

Data cleaning is performed to improve data quality and accuracy.

This step includes:
- Checking for missing values
- Removing duplicate records

Clean data helps produce more reliable analysis results.
"""

# check missing values
print(df.isnull().sum())

# remove duplicates
df.drop_duplicates(inplace=True)

"""# Sales and Profit Analysis

This step calculates the total sales and total profit generated by the business.

These values help measure the overall business performance.
"""

total_sales = df['Sales'].sum()
total_profit = df['Profit'].sum()

print("Total Sales:", total_sales)
print("Total Profit:", total_profit)

"""# Monthly Revenue Trend Analysis

The Order Date column is converted into datetime format for time-based analysis.

Monthly sales trends are analyzed using a line chart to identify:
- High sales periods
- Revenue growth patterns
- Seasonal trends
"""

df['Order Date'] = pd.to_datetime(df['Order Date'])

monthly_sales = df.groupby(df['Order Date'].dt.month)['Sales'].sum()

monthly_sales.plot(marker='o')
plt.title("Monthly Revenue Trend")
plt.xlabel("Month")
plt.ylabel("Sales")
plt.grid()
plt.show()

"""# Top Selling Products Analysis

This analysis identifies the top 10 products with the highest sales revenue.

The visualization helps understand which products contribute most to business sales.
"""

top_products = df.groupby('Product Name')['Sales'].sum().sort_values(ascending=False).head(10)

top_products.plot(kind='bar')
plt.title("Top 10 Selling Products")
plt.xlabel("Products")
plt.ylabel("Sales")
plt.show()

"""# Category Performance Analysis

Sales performance across different product categories is analyzed using a pie chart.

This helps identify categories with:
- Highest sales contribution
- Strong market performance
"""

category_sales = df.groupby('Category')['Sales'].sum()

category_sales.plot(kind='pie', autopct='%1.1f%%')
plt.title("Category Performance")
plt.ylabel("")
plt.show()

"""# Regional Sales Performance

Sales performance is compared across different regions using a bar chart.

This analysis helps identify:
- High-performing regions
- Low-performing regions
- Regional business opportunities
"""

region_sales = df.groupby('Region')['Sales'].sum()

sns.barplot(x=region_sales.index, y=region_sales.values)

plt.title("Regional Sales Performance")
plt.xlabel("Region")
plt.ylabel("Sales")
plt.show()

"""# Profit Analysis by Category

This chart compares profit generated by different product categories.

It helps identify categories that contribute most to business profitability.
"""

sns.barplot(x='Category', y='Profit', data=df)
plt.title("Profit by Category")
plt.show()

"""# State-wise Sales Analysis

This analysis identifies the top-performing states based on sales revenue.

The visualization helps understand geographical sales distribution and business opportunities.
"""

state_sales = df.groupby('State')['Sales'].sum().sort_values(ascending=False).head(10)

state_sales.plot(kind='bar')
plt.title("Top States by Sales")
plt.show()
